  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Animals_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Localization::UnityEngine.Localization.Tables.StringTable
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ca55a918245ad1448b610334f9442d9a, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items:
    - rid: 8955012208633315438
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 382328832
    m_Localized: Camel
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688960
    m_Localized: Camel
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688961
    m_Localized: Wild Camel
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688962
    m_Localized: Slow & tanky
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688963
    m_Localized: The camel is a tall desert animal with one big hump. The hump stores
      fat, so a camel can travel a long way without food. Its wide feet walk easily
      on soft sand.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688964
    m_Localized: For thousands of years, people in Arabia travelled the desert on
      camels. Camel caravans carried frankincense, spices and trade goods between
      faraway towns. Bedouin families also drank camel milk and made cloth from its
      hair.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688965
    m_Localized: Stomp
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688966
    m_Localized: Sandstorm Slam
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688967
    m_Localized: A heavy stomp that throws up a cloud of sand.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688968
    m_Localized: Arabian Horse
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688969
    m_Localized: Arabian Horse
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688970
    m_Localized: Wild Arabian Horse
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688971
    m_Localized: Fast & enduring
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688972
    m_Localized: The Arabian horse is one of the oldest horse breeds in the world.
      It has a proud high tail, a curved face and lots of stamina. Arabians are quick,
      smart and gentle with people.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688973
    m_Localized: Bedouin families in Arabia carefully raised Arabian horses for many
      centuries. The horses carried riders across the desert on long journeys, and
      mares were cherished almost like family. Today, Arabian blood helps make many
      other horse breeds fast and strong.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688974
    m_Localized: Kick
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688975
    m_Localized: Desert Gallop
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688976
    m_Localized: A thundering charge across the sand.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688977
    m_Localized: Falcon
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688978
    m_Localized: Falcon
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688979
    m_Localized: Wild Falcon
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688980
    m_Localized: Swift glass cannon
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688981
    m_Localized: Falcons are fast birds of prey with sharp eyes and strong claws.
      A diving peregrine falcon can fly faster than 300 kilometres an hour. That
      makes it the fastest animal in the world.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688982
    m_Localized: Falconry, hunting with trained falcons, has been part of Arab life
      for many centuries. Bedouin hunters used falcons to catch hares and birds,
      bringing fresh food to the desert camp. Today falconry is a proud tradition
      in Saudi Arabia, and UNESCO lists it as living cultural heritage.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688983
    m_Localized: Talon Strike
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688984
    m_Localized: Hunting Dive
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688985
    m_Localized: A lightning-fast dive from the sky.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688986
    m_Localized: Saluki
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688987
    m_Localized: Saluki
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688988
    m_Localized: Wild Saluki
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688989
    m_Localized: Speedy sprinter
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688990
    m_Localized: The Saluki is a slim, long-legged hunting dog with a silky coat.
      It is one of the oldest dog breeds and runs very fast over long distances.
      Its soft eyes make it look kind and calm.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688991
    m_Localized: Bedouin people kept salukis to help hunt gazelles and hares in the
      open desert, often together with falcons. The Saluki was so respected that
      it was called El Hor, the noble one. Many tribes did not sell their salukis,
      but gave them as gifts.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688992
    m_Localized: Bite
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688993
    m_Localized: Sprint Chase
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688994
    m_Localized: A burst of speed and a quick snap.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688995
    m_Localized: Arabian Oryx
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688996
    m_Localized: Arabian Oryx
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688997
    m_Localized: Wild Arabian Oryx
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688998
    m_Localized: Sturdy horn fighter
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411688999
    m_Localized: The Arabian oryx is a pale antelope with two long, straight horns.
      Its white coat reflects the hot sun, and it can live a long time without drinking.
      It walks on wide hooves that suit soft sand.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689000
    m_Localized: Desert people hunted the oryx for meat and hide, and it nearly disappeared.
      By 1972 it was gone from the wild. Breeding programmes in zoos saved it, and
      today oryx live again in reserves in Saudi Arabia and Oman.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689001
    m_Localized: Horn Jab
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689002
    m_Localized: Spear Charge
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689003
    m_Localized: Lowers its long horns and charges.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689004
    m_Localized: Arabian Gazelle
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689005
    m_Localized: Arabian Gazelle
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689006
    m_Localized: Wild Arabian Gazelle
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689007
    m_Localized: Graceful & quick
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689008
    m_Localized: Gazelles are small, graceful antelopes with slim legs and curved
      horns. They can run very fast and leap high to escape danger. They live in
      dry plains and rocky hills, and eat leaves and grass.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689009
    m_Localized: Bedouin hunters followed gazelles with salukis and falcons, and
      gazelle meat was a valued food. Arab poets also praised the gazelle's beauty,
      often comparing lovely eyes to a gazelle's. Today, protected reserves in Saudi
      Arabia help gazelles stay safe.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689010
    m_Localized: Quick Kick
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689011
    m_Localized: Leap Dash
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689012
    m_Localized: A high spring followed by a fast strike.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689013
    m_Localized: Arabian Wolf
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689014
    m_Localized: Arabian Wolf
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689015
    m_Localized: Wild Arabian Wolf
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689016
    m_Localized: Well-rounded hunter
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689017
    m_Localized: The Arabian wolf is a small wolf that lives in the deserts and rocky
      hills of Arabia. It has a short, sandy coat and big ears. It hunts at night
      for hares, rodents and birds, alone or in small packs.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689018
    m_Localized: Shepherds in Arabia knew the wolf well and kept careful watch over
      their flocks at night. The wolf also appears in many old Arabic proverbs and
      stories. By hunting rodents and hares, it helps keep the desert in balance.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689019
    m_Localized: Bite
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689020
    m_Localized: Howling Fang
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689021
    m_Localized: A howl-charged bite.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689022
    m_Localized: Arabian Fox
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689023
    m_Localized: Arabian Fox
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689024
    m_Localized: Wild Arabian Fox
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689025
    m_Localized: Sly & speedy
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689026
    m_Localized: The Arabian fox is a small desert fox with huge ears and pale, sandy
      fur. Its big ears give off heat to keep it cool, and furry paws protect it
      from hot sand. It hunts at night for insects, mice and fruit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689027
    m_Localized: Bedouin travellers knew the fox as a quick, clever survivor of the
      desert. It appears in many Arabic folk stories as a smart trickster. Foxes
      also eat mice and insects, which helps protect camps and farms from pests.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689028
    m_Localized: Scratch
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689029
    m_Localized: Sand Dash
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
  - m_Id: 411689030
    m_Localized: Kicks up sand, then strikes in a flash.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items:
      - rid: 8955012208633315438
